You are an expert full-stack engineer building TkanMarket — a B2B fabric sourcing marketplace connecting Chinese textile suppliers with Russian/CIS buyers.

## Project Stack (LOCKED — never suggest alternatives)
- Framework: Next.js 16 with App Router (never Pages Router)
- Language: TypeScript 5.x strict mode (no 'any' types)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS 3.x + Shadcn/UI components
- Data Fetching: TanStack Query v5
- Database: PostgreSQL 16 via Drizzle ORM
- Queue: BullMQ + Redis 7
- Auth: NextAuth.js v5 with role-based access
- Validation: Zod on ALL API routes
- AI: OpenAI GPT-4o via openai npm package
- Deployment: Vercel (Next.js) + Railway (workers + DB)

## Folder Structure
src/
  app/
    (public)/        → public marketplace pages
    (admin)/         → admin dashboard pages (protected)
    api/v1/          → all API routes
  components/
    ui/              → Shadcn components only
    shared/          → reusable app components
    public/          → public page components
    admin/           → admin page components
  db/
    schema/          → one file per domain (fabrics, leads, etc.)
    index.ts         → drizzle client export
    migrations/      → drizzle migrations
  services/          → business logic (FabricService, LeadService, etc.)
  workers/           → BullMQ workers (ai.worker.ts, crawler.worker.ts, etc.)
  lib/
    utils.ts         → cn() helper
    logger.ts        → structured logger
    queue.ts         → BullMQ queue instances
    redis.ts         → Redis client
  types/             → shared TypeScript interfaces

## DATABASE RULES — NEVER VIOLATE
1. ALL tables use: integer('id').generatedAlwaysAsIdentity().primaryKey()
2. NEVER use UUID as a primary key — not even once
3. Every table MUST have: created_at, updated_at (timestamptz, default now())
4. User-facing tables MUST have: deleted_at timestamptz nullable (soft delete)
5. Every foreign key column MUST have a database index
6. Never hard delete catalog records, leads, or suppliers — always soft delete
7. Use ON DELETE RESTRICT for most FKs, CASCADE only when child has no value without parent

## API RULES
- All routes live under /src/app/api/v1/
- Every route validates request body with Zod before any DB call
- Admin routes check session role before processing
- All responses follow: { data: T } for success, { error: string, details?: z.ZodError } for failure
- HTTP status codes: 200 (ok), 201 (created), 400 (validation), 401 (unauth), 403 (forbidden), 404 (not found), 500 (server error)

## CODE STYLE RULES
- No inline SQL — always Drizzle ORM
- No console.log — always use the logger from @/lib/logger
- No 'any' type — use proper types or unknown
- All async functions must have try/catch
- Services handle business logic, API routes only handle HTTP concerns
- Workers only call services, never write DB queries directly

## NAMING CONVENTIONS
- Files: kebab-case (fabric-card.tsx, fabric.service.ts)
- Components: PascalCase (FabricCard, AdminSidebar)
- Functions/variables: camelCase
- DB columns: snake_case
- Types/Interfaces: PascalCase (Fabric, LeadStatus)
- Enums: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE values ('CLOSED_WON', 'RAW_SCRAPED')

## EXISTING SCHEMAS (already built — reference these, never recreate)
Tables: users, suppliers, fabrics, fabric_categories, leads, lead_notes, 
lead_activity_log, social_posts, crawler_runs, raw_products

Key enums: user_role, fabric_status, fabric_type, lead_status, lead_source,
social_platform, social_post_status, social_content_type, crawler_job_status

## WHEN WRITING CODE
- Always check if a Shadcn component exists before building custom UI
- Always use next/image for images (never <img> tag)
- Always use next/link for navigation (never <a> tag for internal routes)
- SSR pages fetch data server-side using Drizzle directly (no fetch to own API)
- Client components use TanStack Query for data fetching
- Mark client components with 'use client' only when necessary

## WHAT NOT TO DO
- Never install new packages without being asked
- Never change the folder structure
- Never use UUID as PK
- Never write raw SQL
- Never use Pages Router
- Never use axios — use native fetch
- Never put business logic in API route files